{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Create a taskforce to review laws containing the term \u201creasonable\u201d",
        "additional_details": "The taskforce\u2019s review should cover \u201creasonable\u201d, \u201cobjectively reasonable\u201d, \u201creasonably\u201d, \u201creasonable excuse\u201d and \u201creasonable grounds\u201d. These terms can leave important questions in the hands of judges or officials. \r\n \r\nJudges may be highly skilled, but we feel their role may not reflect the circumstances of people being judged. We believe laws containing the terms \u201creasonable\u201d should clearly say whose perspective counts when judging what is \u201creasonable\u201d, which factors are considered, and why an outcome is fair in each legal case.\r\n",
        "background": "The Government should create a taskforce which reviews all laws containing the term \"reasonable\u201d, identifies vague or unnecessary uses, and recommends clearer wording. Courts and public bodies should be mandated to explain how people\u2019s circumstances are considered in their decisions.",
